            "k",
            "k",
            "k",
            "k"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "ScriptedTarget": {
      "description": "What a ScriptedAction acts on (06 §20 target; 21 §7 TargetSpec): one inspectable detail, by its room and its key in that room's details, offered only while the actor is in that room; or (toolbox row G4) a use: a tool the actor holds, used on another item on the floor of the actor's room or carried directly, both chosen by the invocation (perform item_id and target_id), the scripted action keyed by the tool's properties here and the target's through its policy (has_tag and status_active, subject target), never by item ids; or (toolbox row 29a) a spell named by its word, castable by an actor only while its learned fact reads true for them.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "kind": {
              "const": "detail"
            },
            "room": {
              "$ref": "identity.schema.json#/$defs/DefinitionRef"
            },
            "detail": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Key"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "kind",
            "room",
            "detail"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "kind": {
              "const": "use"
            },
            "tool": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/UseTool"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "kind",
            "tool"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        {
          "description": "Toolbox row 29a (word bar S2): a spell, cast only by the cast command typing its word (no other spell scripted action has it), never offered by key or performed; it acts on the caster's body. With aimed (loka-x6t.109) it is cast at one entity in those scopes of the caster's room or body (cast target_id; invalid_target otherwise, after the word's own invalid_state), its policy read with that target, offered on each admitted target's GameView entry and never in spell_words; an unaimed spell refuses a target_id. learned names a bool fact of this cartridge (FACT_TYPE_MISMATCH otherwise; a per_subject fact is FACT_SCOPE_UNSUPPORTED, loader only): while it reads false for the caster, a cast of the word is refused exactly as an unknown word and GameView spell_words omits it.",
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "kind": {
              "const": "spell"
            },
            "word": {
              "$ref": "dialogue.schema.json#/$defs/SpokenKeyword"
            },
            "learned": {
              "$ref": "identity.schema.json#/$defs/DefinitionRef"
            },
            "aimed": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "scopes": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "enum": ["room_occupants", "room_contents", "inventory"]
                  },
                  "minItems": 1
                }
              },
              "required": ["scopes"],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "kind",
            "word",
            "learned"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "kind": "detail",
          "room": {
            "cartridge_id": "recipe_sampler",
            "cartridge_version": "0.0.1",
            "kind": "room",
            "key": "belfry"
          },
          "detail": "bell"
        },
        {
          "kind": "use",
          "tool": {
            "tag": "liquid_holding",
            "liquid": {
              "cartridge_id": "use_sampler",
              "cartridge_version": "0.0.1",
              "kind": "liquid",
              "key": "water"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "UseTool": {
      "description": "Toolbox row G4: what a use scripted action's tool must be, at least one property: an item whose definition declares tag, and a vessel holding some of liquid (quantity above 0).",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "tag": {"description":"A tag the tool item definition declares.",
          "$ref": "entity.schema.json#/$defs/Tag"
        },
        "liquid": {"description":"A liquid the tool vessel holds some of.",
          "$ref": "identity.schema.json#/$defs/DefinitionRef"
        }
      },
      "requiredUnless": {
        "tag": [
          "liquid"
        ]
      },
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "examples": [
        {
          "tag": "metal"
        }
      ]
    },
    "ScriptedAction": {
      "description": "A cartridge-local action composed only of registered operations (06 §20 Composed actions / ScriptedAction; 21 §7; 05 §28), invoked by the perform command: its stable key (its ActionSet identity), name, the aliases a player types as its verb (the first words of the command), its target, presentation priority, availability policy (evaluated for the actor; while it fails the action is shown unavailable and perform is rejected), and its outcomes. success is one explicit list of at most 16 steps, run in order as one logical decision (04 §5.2) and followed by the engine's action_completed event, and the narration its actor reads; observers is the line others in the room would read, kept for the first host with a second viewer. Optional (R5 S6): a check (step.schema.json Check; check@1), whose result selects the outcome: success when it passes, failure when it fails; a scripted action has a failure outcome exactly when it has a check (OUTCOME_MISMATCH). A failed check is an accepted perform with outcome failure whose RNG draw and time commit like success (04 §5.0); a scripted action without a check has outcome performed. failure's steps may be empty. duration, a whole number of LogicalTime units, advances the clock by that much on every accepted perform, success or failure (21 §7 Cost, time; 04 §5.4: one time.advance after the outcome's steps); events keep the time the perform was admitted at. action_completed follows the outcome's steps when the outcome is performed or success, never failure. Optional (R5 S6b): costs (ActionCost, resource@1), paid in order by the actor's body on every admitted perform, failure included; one it cannot pay rejects the perform insufficient_resource before any check or draw. cooldown, a whole number of LogicalTime units: a perform by the same actor before the last admitted attempt's time plus cooldown is rejected cooldown; an admitted attempt, failure included, starts it at its admission time (delta cooldown.start), and at exactly that time plus cooldown the scripted action is available again. Admission order: target, cooldown, costs, then the check. Optional (toolbox row W23, fact@1): tip, a text the actor reads once, after the outcome's narration, on the first accepted perform (success, failure or performed); that perform also assigns the engine-owned player fact seen_tip_<key> (bool, default false) true, which the compiler adds, so a scripted action with a tip has a key of at most 55 characters and no definition writes that fact (RESERVED_FACT). Optional (loka-j64e): reason, a text key the GameView adds as the message of an offered ActionSet action's (or learned spell word's) unavailable reason while its policy fails (a use-target scripted action is hidden then, so its reason is not shown); the perform or cast refusal stays invalid_state. Optional (Homestead hs-10): craft (ActionCraft), the items a station scripted action uses up and makes; a spell scripted action has none (SCHEMA_VIOLATION). Result bands join later.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "key": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Key"
        },
        "name": {"description":"Text key of its name.",
          "$ref": "text.schema.json#/$defs/TextKey"
        },
        "aliases": {"description":"Words a player types as its verb.",
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "room.schema.json#/$defs/Alias"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "maxItems": 16
        },
        "target": {"description":"Its target.",
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ScriptedTarget"
        },
        "priority": {"description":"Presentation priority.",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "policy": {
          "$ref": "policy.schema.json#/$defs/Policy"
        },
        "outcomes": {"description":"The outcomes a perform selects.",
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "success": {"description":"Runs when the check passes, or when the action has no check.",
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "steps": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "step.schema.json#/$defs/Step"
                  },
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "maxItems": 16
                },
                "narration": {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/ActionNarration"
                },
